    guideTitle: "GUIDE : CAPABILITY VS PERFORMANCE",
    guideIntro: "### Methodology Selection\nChoice depends on study purpose, process maturity, and customer requirements.\n\n#### **1. Machine Capability (Cm / Cmk)**\nFocuses on the machine's inherent technical potential under controlled conditions (n=50).\n*   **Cm Formula**: (USL - LSL) / (6 * s_total)\n*   **Cmk Formula**: min((USL - Mean) / (3 * s_total), (Mean - LSL) / (3 * s_total))\n\n#### **2. Process Performance (Pp / Ppk)**\nDescribes actual ability over time, considering all sources of variation (6M).\n*   **Pp Formula**: (USL - LSL) / (6 * s_total)\n*   **Ppk Formula**: min((USL - Mean) / (3 * s_total), (Mean - LSL) / (3 * s_total))\n\n#### **3. Process Capability (Cp / Cpk)**\nCalculated for processes in statistical control. Shows inherent capability.\n*   **Cp Formula**: (USL - LSL) / (6 * σ_within)\n*   **Cpk Formula**: min((USL - Mean) / (3 * σ_within), (Mean - LSL) / (3 * σ_within))",
